- Add opt-in expiry payouts with `expiry_payouts`, disabled by default.
  At tree expiry the watchman pays each customer VTXO on-chain to `tr(M)`,
  where M is the owner mailbox key recorded when the VTXO was created. The
  mode is fixed when the database is created, and a server started in the
  other mode refuses to run. With payouts disabled, the server behaves as
  upstream.
  [#90](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/90)
- Charge a fallback fee of 2,000 sats or 1%, whichever is larger, once per
  expired tree. A payout too small to cover the fee is forfeited. The operator
  pays miner fees and replaces stuck payouts. Owner outputs can never exceed
  the value of the tree they sweep, and an error on one tree does not stop the
  others.
  [#90](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/90)
- Pay unregistered boards to their owner, and refund an undelivered arkoor
  to its sender.
  [#90](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/90)
- Report a decided VTXO as `Spent`, with its `FallbackPayout`: pending,
  paid after six confirmations, or forfeited, with the fee and amount paid.
  [#90](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/90)
- Keep Lightning payments safe across expiry payouts. A Lightning send needs
  one owner signature per source VTXO, and a retry is acknowledged by its
  intent. The watchman claims an exited send only with a preimage from that
  source's own payment.
  [#90](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/90)
- Pay invoices directly by arkoor, opt-in with `ln_receive_ark_address_hints`.
  The invoice carries the receiver's Ark address in its route hints. A
  compatible payer on the same server pays it by arkoor through
  `RequestLightningReceiveArkoorCosign`, which settles the receive and makes
  the invoice unpayable. With expiry payouts, the payment must go to the
  receive's mailbox.
  [#90](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/90)
- Refuse an expiry payout or replacement above
  `watchman.expiry_payout_max_fee_rate`, 1,000 sat/vB by default.
  The payout stays pending and is retried on the next pass.
  [#90](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/90)
- Keep the payout schema in its own migration history,
  `scuttle_schema_history`, so upstream migrations never collide with it.
  A database created before this change must be recreated.
  [#90](https://github.com/BullishNode/scuttle/pull/90)
